Late on Thursday evening, I return to my flat.
I usually go to play badminton every Thursday at half past five.
I am coming back after returning the racket at the club.
Just then, a knock is heard on the door.
I open the door.
My neighbour Anitha is standing outside.
"Maya, I must travel this weekend," Anitha says.
"I have a small favor to ask of you."
"What is it, Anitha?" I ask.
"Can you look after my dog Tommy this weekend?" she asks.
"He must not be left alone for whole days," she says.
I happily agree to do that favor.
"I can certainly look after him, I like dogs very much," I say.
"There is a dog at my home in Mexico too."
"I will look after him, Anitha, please do not worry," I say.
"Thank you very much Maya, I will bring him tomorrow evening," Anitha says with a smile.
I am looking forward to spending time with Tommy this weekend.
